# Response headers for the deployed Worker. Cloudflare parses this file out of
# the assets directory and never serves it; `wrangler.jsonc` points that
# directory at `dist/`, and Astro copies everything in `public/` into it.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. Cloudflare's static-asset server sends
# `cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` on everything it has not
# been told otherwise about — content-hashed `/_astro/*` files included. Every
# navigation on this site is a full document load, because `prefetch: false` in
# astro.config.ts is deliberate and there is no client router, so that default
# made a browser revalidate all four webfonts on every single click before it
# was allowed to paint a word in them. Until the answer came back
# `font-display: swap` painted the fallback, which is 25% narrower than IBM
# Plex Mono — so the header, the buttons, the labels and every code block
# reflowed once per link.
#
# scripts/check-webfont-delivery.ts holds this: it serves `dist/` through
# Cloudflare's default and then applies the rules below, so a deleted line here
# fails as the reader's experience of it rather than as a missing file.

# Everything Vite emits under this path carries a content hash in its filename,
# so the bytes behind a given URL can never change. That is the precondition
# `immutable` asks for, and it is a property of the build rather than a promise
# made here: a changed file is a changed hash is a different URL.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# NOT the HTML. A page's URL is stable while its content is not, so `dist/`'s
# documents keep Cloudflare's revalidating default and a deploy is visible on
# the next click. Nothing below overrides them; this comment exists so that the
# absence reads as a decision rather than an omission.
